WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.969
-The House held its latest
impeachment hearing today

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.206
as President Trump's
allies doubled down

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.008
on a ludicrous
conspiracy theory about Ukraine.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.411
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:16.115
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.683
This morning,
the House Judiciary Committee

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:18.985
held its second hearing,

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.986
laying out the impeachment
evidence against Trump.

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:22.422
Now, as we've established,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.324
Republicans have
no counter argument

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.925
on the actual merits
of the case.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.627
For example,
they're so desperate

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.863
that this morning
on Fox News, Republican minority

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.066
leader Kevin McCarthy argued
that you shouldn't be allowed

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:36.502
to impeach a president
in their first term.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:37.836
-In modern history
we've never gone

00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:40.039
after impeaching a president
in the first term.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.942
-Is that really your argument?

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.977
We shouldn't impeach him
because it's his first term?

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:48.781
Everyone knows the founders said
you can commit unlimited crimes

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.018
until your second term.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.786
Republicans can't contest
any of the facts,

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.388
so instead,
during the hearing today,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.591
they tried to stall by staging
as many dumb interruptions

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:02.695
as possible and forcing Chairman
Jerry Nadler to gavel them down.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.130
-The House committee
on the Judiciary

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.431
will come to order.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.032
Without objection the chair
is authorized

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:08.567
to declare recesses
of the committee --

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.969
-I object.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.504
-Objection noted.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.906
[ Gavel bangs ]
Without objection --

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.375
-Ruling on the point of order --
-You made a --

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.343
You made a ruling on the point
of order, Mr. Chairman.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.145
You can't then
not allow us to --

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.412
-The gentleman
is not recognized.

00:01:20.412 --> 00:01:21.580
[ Gavel bangs ]
-It's a rule.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.816
-The obligation,
not the consideration.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.285
You are obligated --
-Those are not in debate.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:28.921
Suspend.
Gentleman is not recognized.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.023
-...gets the chance
to offer rebuttal.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.192
Nobody asked for this --
[ Gavel banging ]

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.661
-The gentleman will suspend.
[ Gavel banging ]

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.229
-Bang it harder.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.563
-The gentleman will suspend.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:39.399
-Will you let him finish
his point of order?

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.733
-He made his point of order.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.569
-The gentleman will suspend
and not make a speech.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.773
-Man, that gavel
is getting a workout.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.108
When this is over,
Jerry Nadler is going to have

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.712
one giant hulk arm.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.914
Republicans had to engage
in these dumb stunts

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.115
because they have nothing else.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.483
For example, they also demanded

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.252
that House
Intelligence Committee chairman

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.487
Adam Schiff, who conducted
the first round of hearings,

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.756
testify during today's hearing,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.759
and to really hammer the point
home, they brought in a poster

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.796
that said, where is Adam,
and another poster with Schiff's

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.530
face on the side
of a milk carton.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:12.832
Why?

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.101
Why do these look like
middle school art projects?

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.803
I mean, can't the Republicans

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.904
hire someone
who is good at graphic design?

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:21.107
This looks like something
a crazy guy would wear

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.210
on a sandwich board
in Times Square.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.545
This of course follows
the GOP's proud tradition

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:29.415
of bringing very stupid posters
to official House proceedings,

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.217
like the time they made a poster
that said,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.420
"Liar, liar pants on fire"
for Michael Cohen's testimony,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.755
or the time they brought
in a poster

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.257
accusing Democrats
of acting like

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.924
Soviets during
the first impeachment vote.

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.493
At this point, Republicans

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:44.396
are the only thing keeping
the D.C. Kinko's in business.

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:47.232
If you walk into Kinko's now,
their price list includes black

00:02:47.232 --> 00:02:51.036
and white copies, color copies,
dumb Republican posters.

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:53.205
Now, the main point
of the hearing today

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:55.508
was to let lawyers for Democrats
and Republicans

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.244
lay out their cases, and the
Republican lawyer was a guy

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.912
you might remember
from the first round

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.048
of impeachment hearings,
Steve Castor.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:05.885
In those hearings, Castor often
struggled to question witnesses.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.154
At one point during the first
round of hearings,

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.089
his line of questioning
was so bad

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:13.626
it flustered the witness
and left him speechless.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:18.364
-In fairness, this irregular
channel of diplomacy,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:24.169
it's not as outlandish
as it could be, is that correct?

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:26.105
-It's not as outlandish
as it could be.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:29.775
It is a little unusual for
the U.S. Ambassador to the EU

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:33.212
to play a role
in Ukraine policy.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:35.014
-Okay.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.315
And, you know,
might be irregular

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.251
but it is
certainly not outlandish.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:42.322
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:43.623
And then Secretary Perry --

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:47.193
-I mean, that's probably
the same series

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.028
of faces
the Kinko's employee made

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.364
when Republicans asked him
to print those dumb posters.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.866
"Can you put this man's face
on a milk carton?

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.100
It's for Congress."

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:59.204
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:04.477
So that -- that's the guy.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:07.246
That's the guy Republicans had
making their arguments today.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.248
Now, let's compare
the Democrats' lawyer,

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:12.418
who presented a lengthy body
of evidence, witness testimony,

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.354
and video evidence to Castor.
the Republicans' lawyer.

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:18.925
-President Trump's persistent
and continuing effort

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:22.494
to coerce a foreign country
to help him cheat to win

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:26.032
an election is a clear
and present danger

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.935
to our free and fair elections
and to our national security.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:33.206
-To impeach a president
who 63 million people voted

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:39.845
for over eight lines
in a call transcript is baloney.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:42.814
-It's, uh, baloney.

00:04:42.814 --> 00:04:44.250
Really loses the drama

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.588
when the word you're
ramping up to is baloney.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.923
You ever hear a detective
in a mystery novel saying,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:56.061
"I've deduced that the suspect's
alibi is, uh, baloney."

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:58.931
Castor's demeanor throughout
this whole thing

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:02.168
was that of a guy who knew
he was fighting a losing battle.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.370
In fact, instead of keeping his
documents in a brief case

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.238
or cardboard boxes
like most lawyers,

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.573
he showed up
to the hearing this morning

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:11.477
with his papers
in a grocery store tote bag.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.945
Look at that.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.680
It's like he forgot about the
hearing until the last minute

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.816
and had to find whatever
was lying around his house.

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:20.486
I bet there was only one piece
of paper at the top of that bag

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.956
and the rest of it
was just organic produce.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.559
And the fact that he kept all
of his papers in a grocery bag

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.860
might explain why he didn't seem

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.595
to know very much
about what was in them.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.165
The Republicans wrote
their own report

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.565
rebutting
the impeachment inquiry.

00:05:33.565 --> 00:05:36.502
But when Castor was questioned
by the Democratic counsel

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.303
about a key element
of that report,

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:40.439
he didn't seem to know
anything about it.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.341
-Quote, "I thought
that the references

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.709
to specific individuals

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:46.378
and investigations such
as former Vice President Biden

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:50.216
and his son struck me
as political in nature.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.717
Given that former Vice President

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:54.253
is a political opponent
of the President."

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:58.390
So you left that out of your
staff report, too, didn't you?

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.594
-Well, you know,
Miss Williams --

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:04.029
-Sir, did you leave that out
of your report? Yes or no?

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:06.466
-I -- if you're telling me
I did --

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.400
I don't know as I sit here
right now that's in the report.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.369
-I'm telling you you did.
-Okay.

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:15.241
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.742
-I have my report in my bag.

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:17.877
Just let me --

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.446
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:24.150
[ Applause ]

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.296
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:42.168
"You guys, I think
I brought my groceries."

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.570
What we saw yet again today is
that the Republican Party and

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.105
Donald Trump is fundamentally
untethered from reality,

00:06:47.105 --> 00:06:49.375
and my favorite recent example
of this came on Friday

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.210
when Trump was
at the White House

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.013
talking about repealing
environmental regulations,

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:57.917
and he said this truly
bat[bleep] about toilets.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:01.053
-We have a situation where
we're looking very strongly

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:06.392
at sinks and showers
and other elements of bathrooms

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:10.295
where you turn the faucet
on and areas

00:07:10.295 --> 00:07:11.997
where there is tremendous
amounts of water

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:13.932
where the water
rushes out to sea

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:16.969
because you could never handle
it and you don't get any water.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:19.605
You turn on the faucet.
You don't get any water.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:23.542
They take a shower and water
comes dripping out,

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:27.479
just dripping out,
very quietly dripping out.

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:29.548
People are flushing toilets
10 times,

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:32.618
15 times
as opposed to once.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:33.919
-Hey, man.

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:37.823
Just because you have
to flush 10 or 15 times

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:39.057
doesn't mean everyone does.

00:07:39.057 --> 00:07:40.526
I mean, look at your diet.

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:45.064
Standard toilets were not built
to withstand this.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:47.666
I bet the White House toilets
are like the theme park models

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:48.901
that will suck down anything.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.569
You know, when you flush them,
they sound

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:53.038
like an F-14 taking off.

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:54.873
I bet at least once a day
the Secret Service

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.242
knocks on the bathroom door
and says,

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:58.110
"Mr. President,
you still in there?

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.145
It's been over an hour,"
and then he says, "Hold on.

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:01.280
I'll be right out."

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:04.850
[ Toilet flushes ]

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:09.755
[ Applause ]

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.490
"Son of a gun.
I got to flush again."

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:16.695
[ Toilet flushes ]

00:08:16.695 --> 00:08:18.764
My favorite part, though,
came right after that

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.132
when the President said this.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.235
-People are flushing toilets
10 times,

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:25.471
15 times as opposed to once.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.740
They end up using more water,

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:31.744
so EPA is looking at that
very strongly, at my suggestion.

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:34.680
-Oh, was it your suggestion?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.049
I'm pretty sure we all know
where it came from.

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.585
I mean, can you imagine the EPA
going through the suggestion box

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:40.852
at the end of the week?

00:08:40.852 --> 00:08:42.621
Alright.
Bring back casual Fridays.

00:08:42.621 --> 00:08:44.056
Not a terrible idea.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:45.557
Oh, new coffee
for the break room.

00:08:45.557 --> 00:08:46.492
We can do that.

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:47.959
Let's see what we have here.

00:08:47.959 --> 00:08:51.230
Look into toilets that have
to be flushed 15 times.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.266
You turn on the faucet
and you don't get any water.

00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:59.738
You take a shower and water
comes dripping out very quietly.

00:08:59.738 --> 00:09:01.106
Dripping out.

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:03.542
Guys, who told the President
about the suggestion box?!

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:07.346
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:14.153
So, Trump won't tell the EPA
to deal with the climate crisis

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:16.188
that poses an existential threat
to the planet,

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:18.390
but he will tell them
to look into toilets

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.026
that supposedly have to be
flushed 15 times.

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:22.628
But still,
you got to give it to Trump.

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:24.463
He might not know
how toilets work.

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:26.064
He might not care
about the climate crisis.

00:09:26.064 --> 00:09:27.466
But when he is right,
he is right.

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:29.335
And, later at that same event,
the President

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:31.503
said something that even
I cannot criticize

00:09:31.503 --> 00:09:33.205
because it is undeniably true.

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:35.574
-You have many states
where they have so much water

00:09:35.574 --> 00:09:36.975
that it comes down.

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:38.144
It's called rain.

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:42.914
[ Laughter ]

00:09:42.914 --> 00:09:44.683
-Can't argue with the man.

00:09:44.683 --> 00:09:46.585
That's airtight.

00:09:46.585 --> 00:09:48.654
Sounds like the sports guy
on the local news

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:50.156
who had to fill in
for the weather man.

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:52.124
And the clouds, there's
no other way to say it.

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:53.091
They had too much water.

00:09:53.091 --> 00:09:55.493
They're puking water.

00:09:55.493 --> 00:09:58.764
It's also called rain.

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:00.065
This is how detached
from reality

00:10:00.065 --> 00:10:02.301
Trump is, and as we've learned
throughout this

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:03.935
impeachment process,
it's not just him.

00:10:03.935 --> 00:10:06.004
He's brought the entire
Republican Party along with him.

00:10:06.004 --> 00:10:07.406
Just take Texas Senator
Ted Cruz.

00:10:07.406 --> 00:10:09.942
Now, you might remember him
as the guy who grew a beard

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:11.377
and looks like
Santa's deadbeat brother.

00:10:11.377 --> 00:10:13.011
Well, to defend Trump
during the impeachment inquiry,

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:15.647
Republicans have been

00:10:15.647 --> 00:10:17.482
pushing a ludicrous
conspiracy theory

00:10:17.482 --> 00:10:20.418
that Ukraine interfered
in the 2016 election,

00:10:20.418 --> 00:10:23.121
and that is what Trump
was concerned about, so Cruz,

00:10:23.121 --> 00:10:25.925
who was himself the subject
of several Trump conspiracy

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:27.759
theories during the campaign
and even once called

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:29.895
Trump a pathological liar,
went on TV yesterday

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:32.864
and repeated that insane theory
to the shock of

00:10:32.864 --> 00:10:34.500
"Meet the Press" host
Chuck Todd.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.001
-Do you believe Ukraine
meddled in the American

00:10:36.001 --> 00:10:38.370
election in 2016?

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.605
-I do and I think there is
considerable evidence.

00:10:40.605 --> 00:10:42.541
-You do?

00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:44.310
-Wow!

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.411
You know what you just said
is crazy

00:10:46.411 --> 00:10:48.714
when the person you're talking
to reacts like that.

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.315
Like if you were at a party
and someone said

00:10:50.315 --> 00:10:51.650
they hate baby Yoda.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.719
You do?

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.154
But all he does is sip soup.

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:58.323
He doesn't want trouble,
you monster!

00:10:58.323 --> 00:11:01.493
In that interview, Cruz pointed
to an op-ed

00:11:01.493 --> 00:11:02.861
written by a Ukrainian
ambassador

00:11:02.861 --> 00:11:04.663
in 2016 criticizing Trump

00:11:04.663 --> 00:11:07.366
but that's not even close
to the criminal

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:08.667
Russian hacking campaign

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:10.836
and it's not what
Trump was talking about

00:11:10.836 --> 00:11:13.105
in his infamous phone call
with the President of Ukraine.

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:15.840
Trump was repeating
a deranged conspiracy theory

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.277
that the Democrats had somehow
colluded with Ukraine

00:11:18.277 --> 00:11:20.145
to interfere
